{"task_id": "HumanEval/34", "solution": "def unique(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return a new list containing each element exactly once,\n    sorted in ascending order. The input is not modified.\"\"\"\n    # Step 1: Copy the input list to avoid mutation\n    temp_list = list(l)\n    \n    # Step 2: Sort the copied list\n    temp_list.sort()\n    \n    # Step 3: Deduplicate by iterating once over the sorted list\n    result_list = []\n    prev_item = None\n    for item in temp_list:\n        if prev_item is None or item != prev_item:\n            result_list.append(item)\n            prev_item = item\n            \n    return result_list"}
