{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence efficiently without recursion.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1 or n == 3:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n\n    # Initialize with the base cases: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    f0, f1, f2, f3 = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    # Iteratively compute fib4(k) for k from 4 up to n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = f0 + f1 + f2 + f3\n        f0, f1, f2, f3 = f1, f2, f3, next_fib\n    \n    # f3 now holds fib4(n)\n    return f3"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th Fib4 number using an iterative approach.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1 or n == 3:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n\n    # Initialize the first four values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        # Calculate the next fib4 number\n        next_fib4 = a + b + c + d\n        # Shift the values for the next iteration\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_fib4\n    return d"}
