{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "def monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return True is list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\"\"\"\n    if len(l) < 2:\n        return True\n\n    # Determine initial direction by finding the first non-equal pair.\n    increasing = None\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if l[i] > l[i - 1]:\n            increasing = True\n            break\n        elif l[i] < l[i - 1]:\n            increasing = False\n            break\n\n    # If all elements are equal (e.g., [5,5,5]), 'increasing' remains None, which is monotonic.\n    if increasing is None:\n        return True\n\n    # Verify that the rest of the list follows the determined direction.\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if increasing and l[i] < l[i - 1]:\n            return False\n        if not increasing and l[i] > l[i - 1]:\n            return False\n    return True"}
