{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "def anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a string where each word's characters are sorted in ascending ASCII order.\n    The original order of words and spaces is preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_parts = []\n    current_word_start = 0\n\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        if s[i] == ' ':\n            # If we just finished a word before this space\n            if i > current_word_start:\n                word = s[current_word_start:i]\n                result_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(word)))\n            \n            # Append the space itself\n            result_parts.append(' ')\n            \n            # Start tracking the next potential word\n            current_word_start = i + 1\n        \n    # After the loop, if there's a pending word at the end of the string\n    if current_word_start < len(s):\n        word = s[current_word_start:len(s)]\n        result_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(word)))\n\n    return \"\".join(result_parts)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts characters within each word of a string based on specific rules,\n    preserving word order and spaces.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class Word:\n        \"\"\"\n        Represents an alphabetic segment extracted from a raw word.\n        Handles the specific sorting logic for its characters.\n        \"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, text):\n            self.text = text\n        \n        def sort_characters(self):\n            if len(self.text) <= 1:\n                return self.text\n            \n            # Rule: If the segment starts with a lowercase letter, sort all its characters.\n            # Otherwise (starts with an uppercase letter), preserve the first character\n            # and sort the remaining characters.\n            if self.text[0].islower():\n                return \"\".join(sorted(self.text))\n            else:\n                first_char = self.text[0]\n                rest_chars = self.text[1:]\n                return first_char + \"\".join(sorted(rest_chars))\n\n    # The Character class is implicitly handled by Python's string/char operations\n    # as sorted() on a string sorts by ASCII/Unicode value, fulfilling its role.\n\n    result_parts = []\n    \n    # Split the entire string by spaces, capturing the spaces themselves to preserve them.\n    # Example: 'Hello World!!!' -> ['Hello', ' ', 'World!!!']\n    parts = re.split(r'(\\s+)', s)\n\n    for part in parts:\n        if part.isspace(): # If the part is a captured space sequence\n            result_parts.append(part)\n        else: # The part is a 'raw word' which might contain mixed alphabetic and non-alphabetic characters\n            \n            # Split this 'raw word' into contiguous runs of alphabetic and non-alphabetic characters.\n            # Example: 'World!!!' -> ['World', '!!!']\n            segments_in_raw_word = re.findall(r'[a-zA-Z]+|[^a-zA-Z]+', part)\n            \n            non_alphabetic_runs_collected = []\n            processed_alphabetic_runs_collected = []\n\n            for segment_text in segments_in_raw_word:\n                if segment_text.isalpha():\n                    # Process alphabetic runs using the Word entity logic\n                    word_entity = Word(segment_text)\n                    processed_alphabetic_runs_collected.append(word_entity.sort_characters())\n                else:\n                    # Non-alphabetic runs are kept as-is\n                    non_alphabetic_runs_collected.append(segment_text)\n            \n            # Concatenate the processed segments for this raw word.\n            # As per example ('World!!!' -> '!!!Wdlor'), all non-alphabetic parts\n            # precede all processed alphabetic parts in the final assembly.\n            processed_raw_word_output = \"\".join(non_alphabetic_runs_collected) + \\\n                                        \"\".join(processed_alphabetic_runs_collected)\n            \n            result_parts.append(processed_raw_word_output)\n            \n    return \"\".join(result_parts)\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "def get_row(lst, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds integer x in a nested list and returns a list of its (row, column) coordinates.\n    Coordinates are sorted by row ascending, then by column descending.\n    \"\"\"\n    coordinates = []\n    for r_idx, row in enumerate(lst):\n        for c_idx, val in enumerate(row):\n            if val == x:\n                coordinates.append((r_idx, c_idx))\n\n    # Sort primarily by row in ascending order (coord[0])\n    # Secondarily by column in descending order (using -coord[1] to sort ascendingly on the negative value)\n    coordinates.sort(key=lambda coord: (coord[0], -coord[1]))\n    return coordinates"}
