{"task_id": "HumanEval/137", "solution": "def compare_one(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two inputs (int, float, or string representing a real number) and returns\n    the larger value in its original type, or None if they are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _parse_to_float(value):\n        \"\"\"Converts an input to a float, handling string parsing.\"\"\"\n        if isinstance(value, str):\n            # Replace comma with dot for consistent float conversion\n            return float(value.replace(\",\", \".\"))\n        return float(value)\n\n    # Get numeric representations for comparison\n    a_numeric = _parse_to_float(a)\n    b_numeric = _parse_to_float(b)\n\n    # Compare the numeric values and return the original variable if larger\n    if a_numeric > b_numeric:\n        return a\n    elif b_numeric > a_numeric:\n        return b\n    else:\n        # Values are equal\n        return None"}
